sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Cron as cron<br/>(every two hours)
    participant J as judge script
    participant X as frontier model<br/>(Codex CLI, read-only)
    participant L as ledger<br/>(JSONL in git)
    participant G as agent session
    participant W as reflect worker<br/>(Claude subagent)

    Cron->>J: start (a held lock means skip)
    Note over J: slice the agent's transcript since the last run
    J->>X: rubric, what I care about, live extension points,<br/>known families, the slice
    X-->>J: strikes and praise as JSON,<br/>each with quotes and one to three fixes
    J->>L: append verdict rows
    J->>L: verify: a fixed family with no new strike becomes verified
    J->>G: one record with the counts
    G->>W: the open ids
    W->>L: show the verdict, check for a repeat of its family
    Note over W: first fix whose target exists,<br/>a regression test from the strike's quotes,<br/>one local commit
    W->>L: close the row as fixed (or kept for praise)
    alt the next fix needs my authority
        Note over G,W: a repeat whose next fix touches the mission,<br/>a permission, an external write or spending
        W-->>G: the strike goes to my board
    end
    Note over Cron,L: two hours later the next run checks whether the family came back
